      {
        "id": 224069,
        "name": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "username": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/e8c25b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-11-08T14:47:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint, though it was a struggle, and it looked pretty bad until Positive Energy Field healed everyone back up to 13.</p>\n<p>Unlike some here, I had little trouble with zombies. Stabby Knives + Monster of Id killed them all. First round I used Rebel Yell to tell Idealist to kill off the remaining zombies from that initial draw.</p>\n<p>I used Suggestion a few times to put zombies back in the deck. Sure, they heal Gloomy for 5, but I felt delaying any other relics was worth it. Vernal Sonata meant I could bring back Suggestion several times.</p>\n<p>I used Twist the Aether on Chrono Ranger. Sure, it helps Karate Robot, but Chrono Ranger was doing little or nothing with all those 1 point projectile plinks, and Idealist was getting a lot of mileage out of Stabby Knives so I didn’t feel she needed it. The knives, despite being stabby, are still psychic damage.</p>\n<p>Twist the Aether + the bow + Ultimate Target + Hunter and Hunted = 8 points of damage to Gloomy a turn. I never did get a second bounty, so Hunter and Hunted didn’t hurt Chrono Ranger too much.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:21.977Z",
