      {
        "id": 224071,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-11-08T22:46:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint, 14 / 11 / 25 / 10 / 9.</p>\n<p>Nightmist wasn't useless at all for me - she comboed off Vernal Sonata to Heedless Lash (and bounce off herself)&nbsp;4 at Gloomweaver twice, and bounced a couple other hits his way as well.</p>\n<p>Idealist built up a Karate Robot and waited for Twist the Ether.</p>\n<p>Visionary tanked until she had TTE and another Cocoon in hand, broke out of the Cocoon, played TTE on Idealist, then XPW Argent Adept hit her with his base power so she could turtle up immediately. She was regularly blocking 22 damage a round, minimum, from the 5 Zombies and the zombie-focused Cultist, all of which I completely ignored.</p>\n<p>XPWAA hit Chrono-Ranger round 1 to cycle his cards faster, then mostly aimed his base power &nbsp;at Gloomweaver for a relative lack of other things to do. Lots of Vernal Sonata to help out Nightmist, as I said.</p>\n<p>Chrono-Ranger got out the Dart Thrower on round 1 (thanks, Argent Adept), then&nbsp;buried both Acolytes with&nbsp;No Executions. Eventually he got Ultimate Target out, but that just made the Dart Thrower do 2 instead of 1.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Between the hits from Nightmist, plinks from XPWAA and Chrono-Ranger, and plinks from the environment's Bubbles, he was down around the low 40s when Idealist finally cut loose.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
